WEBVTT

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.530
Gareki-kun!

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.790
Akari-sensei, please take care of Nai-chan!

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.380
Gare... ki.

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.680
<i>I must believe... that he's all right!</i>

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.100
Evening Swallow
Score 4

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:17.110
Ga...

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.240
Gareki-kun.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.290
Sapphire Crown.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:36.340
I command stones to bury evil with their dazzling brilliance.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.550
I am known as the Queen of the Crown,

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:43.890
Second Ship Fighter, National Defense Organization, Circus, Iva.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:48.640
Those who do not accept my love shall be smashed to pieces!

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.110
Iva-neesan!

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.160
You fool!

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:08.500
Dork!

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.250
Be thankful to me!

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.300
Can you get up, boy?

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.600
Don't overdo it.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.140
Does it hurt anywhere?

00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:24.140
Do you feel strange anywhere?

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.730
Or feel nauseous?

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:28.980
Sorry.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.400
You're so scared that you can't even talk, right?

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.400
I should have tried harder to protect you!

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.900
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.070
You've got it wrong!

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.450
I'm only silent because I'm trying to figure out what's going on!

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.910
Let go of me!

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.250
Hey, just leave him alone.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.490
Nee-san, why are you here?

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:52.040
I was chasing a Varuga from Gavan.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.000
But he was quick to run away.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.340
Reluctantly, I was going to head back,

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.760
when that Bestial Varuga appeared out of nowhere.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.640
So I decided to take it out on him.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.140
Bestial Varuga?

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.270
It's the beast form of a Varuga.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.270
So that was also...

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.650
Even looking at a man's face doesn't comfort me.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:16.030
It has to be a cute creature.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.770
Didn't Tsukumo come with you?

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.780
In human terms, I would say that it's suffering from bruises..

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.240
Bruises?

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.160
It's okay. It will get better soon.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.750
I wonder if Gareki and Yogi are okay.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:38.720
It's because I acted on my own, isn't it?

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:41.050
You're absolutely right.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.640
However, you aren't the main cause of this.

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.130
The ones who attacked us are.

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.640
<i>Why did they attack Gareki, instead of Nai?</i>

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.360
<i>The examination results showed no signs of Varuga blood cells in either of them.</i>

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.190
There you are.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.450
Akari-sensei!

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.570
Is Gareki injured?

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:10.500
He was reeling.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.450
It was so slow walking along with him.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.130
<i>Why is Iva....</i>

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.170
I'll kiss you if you struggle again.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:21.340
Gareki-kun, it would have been better to be carried on my back.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.970
Please, just kill me.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.430
I don't see any major problems.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.430
But just as a precaution, you should go back to the ship with Iva.

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.440
Gareki, I'm sorry.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.780
Huh? For what?

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.280
Because I...

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.490
Anyway, are you all right?

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.070
Mm-hm.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.330
Well, there were some interruptions,

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.880
but let's get back to our original mission.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:06.390
I hope that there's still something related to Nai and Karoku left.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.600
Ka-Karoku?

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:26.160
So, this is where Nai-chan and Karoku-san stayed.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.660
I'm sorry, but we'll be messing up the place.

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:28.530
Yogi.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:29.330
Roger.

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:55.940
<i>Come, look here.</i>

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.270
<i>Do you understand?</i>

00:06:58.270 --> 00:06:59.860
<i>I understand.</i>

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:01.020
<i>That's good.</i>

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:05.280
Karoku is... warm.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:16.620
It's warm.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:31.890
Karoku-sama,

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:32.890
please get ready.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:50.280
<i>If I touch this light, I wonder if I would cry because of its warmth.</i>

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.660
I'll be right there.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.620
Why did you fail?!

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:03.210
Even if you ask that, Erisyuka-sama, it's not easy when Circus is around.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.760
Karoku showed some interest in that boy, Gareki.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:09.050
I wanted to surprise him by bringing that boy here.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.140
He always has the same expression no matter what I give him.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:15.050
I want him to like me even more.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:18.060
He already likes you very much.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:22.980
Erisyuka-sama is 14 years old and Karoku-sama is 18 years old.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.530
Based on your ages, you two are a great match.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:31.700
I want something more! I want him to forcefully catch me even if I resist!

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.120
I want him to become infatuated with me,

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.950
and desperately want me.

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:40.960
Uro, what should I do?

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:43.870
Let's see... that's a tough one.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.960
There's nothing that interests me.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:53.720
Even Nai-chan said they weren't doing anything out of the ordinary.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:55.890
Right, Nai-chan?

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.390
A bug is coming out.

00:08:58.390 --> 00:08:58.970
A bug?

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:03.440
Sensei?

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.110
Yogi, move this rock.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.060
O-Okay.

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.860
What? Something is...

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.120
Oh, Tsukumo!

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.870
Hooray, it's lunch!

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:27.500
Wow, it's gorgeous.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.170
Did you make this Tsukumo-chan?

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:31.130
It looks so yummy.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.720
Eat quickly.
Here, Nai-chan, sandwiches.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:33.050
Our mission is done.
Here, Nai-chan, sandwiches.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.010
Our mission is done.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:36.510
We're wasting time.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:40.730
Hey, enjoy the food more, Sensei.

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.230
Tsukumo brought them just for us.

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:45.610
Right, Tsukumo?

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:46.730
Iva...

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:50.490
Gareki. Is your wound okay?

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:51.780
I'm not hurt.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:53.240
Just eat your food.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.570
Did you find anything?

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.200
Yes. A notebook.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.660
I took a look inside, but I couldn't understand any of it.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.250
It was all numbers and signs.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:10.090
I'm sorry to say... it's impossible for me to decipher.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:15.340
But, Akari-sensei went through it pretty thoroughly.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.800
I see.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.680
I've a favor to ask of you.

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:31.690
Welcome back. Welcome back.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.700
I'm back.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.160
No way, I'm definitely going!

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:39.530
Hirato-san.
No way, I'm definitely going!

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.620
No you aren't.
Hirato-san.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:41.700
Good afternoon.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.200
I'm going!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.200
We're leaving Niji Forest now.
I'm going!

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.160
I'm telling you... you can't come with me–
We're leaving Niji Forest now.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:50.500
It seems that Karasuna, the place where Gareki-kun used to live, is somewhere nearby,

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.550
so he's saying there's a place he wants to stop by.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:55.170
Let go.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:56.760
Really?

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.390
Are you kidding? Did he say yes?

00:10:58.390 --> 00:10:59.760
Hirato is too nice.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:00.810
He gives me the creeps!

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:04.430
<i>Didn't I report that they were attacked by a Bestial Varuga?</i>

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.810
That's why Yogi is with them.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.900
Iva and Tsukumo, guard the Research Tower group.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.980
Akari-san is there, isn't he?

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:13.810
Let me talk to him.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:18.820
Hirato-san wants to say thank you for various things.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:20.820
There's no need to.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.040
<i>Just hang up.</i>

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:25.200
He's supposed to be a grown-up, right?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.330
What?

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:32.830
"You're such a sweet person, expressing your likes and dislikes in such a straightforward manner."

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:34.960
I'm supposed to tell him that?

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:36.010
No way!

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:38.470
If you want to fight, please do it in person.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:40.880
You two are like cats and dogs.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:44.270
And so that's how it went.

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:48.850
Oh well, I owe you one again.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.450
Good for you, Nai-chan.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:05.320
The captain says you can go with him.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:08.670
He'll just be in my way!

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:12.000
Nai-chan is afraid of being separated from Gareki-kun.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:13.000
What?

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.300
I guess I've got no choice.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.350
Hooray!

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.190
It's been a long time since I wandered around in a town.

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:33.310
Don’t put on a foolish face or your pocket will be picked.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:35.440
That’s like Gareki.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:39.610
Wow, I want that leather bracelet.
Damn it!

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:41.160
Wow, I want that leather bracelet.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:43.660
Can I give it a try?

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:45.080
What?

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:51.960
Huh?

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.170
Why?

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:59.340
Why can't I hit it?

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:01.180
You're pathetic.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:02.430
Give it to me.

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:09.230
Whooooa, you're so cool!

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.320
What? Are you finished with your business?

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.200
Gareki?

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:32.950
Gareki-kun, wait up!

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.590
Gareki?

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:45.260
Eh?

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.090
Tsubame?

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.520
I'm glad.

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:54.600
I'm so happy to see you.

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:09.620
Did something happen?

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:15.540
I... I... I...

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.920
killed a man.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.840
What should I do?

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.810
I didn't know you moved.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:35.310
No wonder you weren't home no matter how many times I visited.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.810
I think it's been around two years since you last came over, right?

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:46.660
Um...

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:48.320
Why...?

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:53.330
Um, what's your relationship with Gareki-kun, Tsubame-chan?

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.960
You're not his little sister... are you?

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:57.380
Relative?

00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:58.540
Um...

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.330
Or maybe his girlfriend?

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:06.180
Y-You're wrong! My dream is to marry a chubby man with gentle eyes!

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.510
That's the total opposite of him, right?

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:14.850
Where is Yotaka?

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:20.320
Um, I haven’t told Yotaka.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:24.730
But, he may already know that something has happened.

00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:30.990
Oh yeah, both of you are twins so you could always sense the other's feelings.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:39.120
Why did you kill?

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.670
<i>Nai-chan, you're too straightforward!</i>

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:47.050
I've always felt sick from time to time.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:50.300
That feeling has gotten worse recently.

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:56.600
I spaced out, and then when I came to, I found blood on my clothes.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.680
I couldn't remember anything.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.570
But it was different yesterday.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:18.330
You bastards, what are you doing to Tsubame!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.710
Stop, you've got it all wrong.

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:22.130
It's Gareki!

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:24.250
Gareki.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:32.260
Oh...You're still alive...

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.350
I wonder if it's okay.

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:39.440
It's a stranger's house after all.

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:43.610
Tsubame said the owner of this house fled away during the night.

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:47.230
Well, that's why I'm asking if we're really doing the right thing.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:52.370
Speaking of which, there aren't many residents in this village.

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:53.950
Has it always been like this?

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:56.740
Of course not.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:03.000
Gareki-kun, what is your relation to those two?

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:08.500
Well, is it okay to ask?

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:18.600
Let's see... I think I was about eight years old, when my parents sold me.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:23.440
I was crowded into the hold of a ship with other kids who were also sold.

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:27.730
And then, it started.

00:17:28.820 --> 00:17:31.110
Senseless bullying of the weak.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:38.120
I wasn't really weak, but I became a target because I was the smallest of everyone.

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:43.160
I was tied up and my two meals per day were taken away.

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:49.170
That's when I noticed there was something strange about those meals.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:52.510
Those kids gradually broke down after a few days...

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:05.610
When I thought I was too tired to walk any more, I was rescued by Tsubaki.

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:11.110
Tsubaki saved my life.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:14.780
And her little brother and sister are Yotaka and Tsubame.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:20.580
Tsubaki was betrayed and killed by a man she loved.

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:23.040
I don't know the face of the man who killed her.

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:27.790
But if I ever meet him, I <i>will</i> kill him.

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:31.550
Huh?

00:18:31.550 --> 00:18:33.050
Can I embrace you?

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.220
What?

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:38.760
The love felt from an embrace, the broken heart of the child will...

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:40.350
You're the child yourself!

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:41.720
I don't like killing.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.390
Gareki, killing is not good.

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:44.520
Gareki-kun!

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:46.850
You two... are so annoying!

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:04.410
<i>I have a brother and a sister about the same age as you.</i>

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:07.170
<i>That's probably why...</i>

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.380
<i>I just couldn't leave you alone.</i>

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:15.300
<i>There's someone I love.</i>

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:18.470
<i>The drug is from him.</i>

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:19.550
<i>It should be safe.</i>

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:21.890
<i>Are you stupid?</i>

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:23.300
<i>Don't trust him.</i>

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:28.150
He got me out of the shop.

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:31.060
He's also paying for Grandpa’s hospital expenses.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.940
<i>It's just a nutritional supplement.</i>

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.570
<i>He said he just wanted data on the twins.</i>

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.530
<i>Aren't you actually suspicious?</i>

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:43.120
<i>That they're being used for some weird experiment.</i>

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:53.250
<i>Because by myself I cannot feed them, protect them, or even buy things they need.</i>

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:56.470
<i>Even for you Gareki, I have nothing...</i>

00:19:56.470 --> 00:19:59.590
<i>I don't need anything.</i>

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:02.600
<i>If it's about money, I'll come up with it somehow.</i>

00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:06.270
<i>So don't you ever go to his place again.</i>

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:11.860
<i>Didn't I tell you not to go?!</i>

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:17.650
Shh.

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:20.400
Outside... Tsubame-chan...

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:28.000
Have you been awake all this time?

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:30.710
Huh? Um well...

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:34.040
You've suspected it ever since you heard Tsubame's story.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.290
I'm... sorry.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:40.840
It's okay. I'd thought of it, too.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:48.760
<i>If Tsubame is...</i>

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.850
<i>Why? When?</i>

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:56.190
<i>Wait, I bet it was those drugs from back then.</i>

00:20:57.280 --> 00:21:01.030
<i>Then, the man who made use of and then killed Tsubaki...</i>

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:07.780
Say, can they possibly return to their original selves?

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:13.000
I understand...

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:19.250
A picture's drawn there.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:21.800
<i>That's not a picture.</i>

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:22.550
<i>That's an injury.</i>

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:26.380
<i>I've seen that pattern somewhere before.</i>

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:31.230
<i>It's similar to the marks on Tsubaki's corpse.</i>

00:21:32.690 --> 00:21:35.320
<i>In that case, it's the same person.</i>

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:40.110
<i>I don't know the face of the man who killed her.</i>

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:43.110
<i>But if I ever meet him, I </i>will<i> kill him.</i>

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:48.490
<i>I will </i> definitely<i> kill him.</i>

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:54.910
Yotaka!

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:27.920
Akari-chan, welcome back.

00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:28.920
Aren't there any souvenirs?

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:31.090
It was work. I didn't go there for a vacation.

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:33.970
Eh? Then what's that in your chest pocket?

00:23:33.970 --> 00:23:35.260
This is a Hana-Usagi.

00:23:35.260 --> 00:23:36.810
That is not fair, Akari-chan!

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:37.890
What's not fair?
